---
// Page-tier St. Charles County cities only. Mention-tier towns stay plain text (no thin city pages).
import { locations, cityHref } from '../../lib/locations';

const county = locations.filter((l) => l.county === 'St. Charles County');
const pages = county.filter((l) => l.tier === 'page');
const mentions = county.filter((l) => l.tier !== 'page');
---
<section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="stc-h">
  <div class="shell stc">
    <h2 id="stc-h" class="display-md">St. Charles County</h2>
    <p>We work across the Missouri River, not only in St. Louis City and St. Louis County. These St. Charles County cities have their own pages:</p>
    <ul>
      {pages.map((l) => (
        <li><a class="link-u accent" href={cityHref(l)}>Junk removal and demolition in {l.name}</a></li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    {mentions.length > 0 && (
      <p>We also serve {mentions.map((l) => l.name).join(', ')}. Those places are on the service-area list, and they don't have city pages yet.</p>
    )}
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  .stc { display: grid; gap: 12px; max-width: 72ch; }
  .stc ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2em; display: grid; gap: 6px; }
</style>
